Expose Router().ResetNetwork() on BoxInstance.

Upstream NekoBox never calls it — the only reference in box.go is commented out
inside Sleep() — and it exposes no way for the host app to call it either. That
leaves Libcore.resetAllConnections(true) as the sole reaction available to an
Android VPN service when the default network changes, and it is not enough:

    // common/conntrack/track.go
    func Close() { ... }                     // closes dialled sockets, nothing else

    // route/router.go
    func (r *Router) ResetNetwork() {
        r.network.ResetNetwork()             // conntrack.Close() + InterfaceUpdated()
        r.dns.ResetNetwork()                 // ClearCache() + close every transport
    }

So after a Wi-Fi <-> mobile handover the DNS transports stay bound to the dead
interface and the DNS cache keeps its stale negative answers. Field diagnostics
show the consequence: twenty-five minutes into a session every single dial began
failing with

    connection: open connection to ... using outbound/vless[proxy]:
        lookup zh.example.com: empty result

while the UI still read "подключено" — the tunnel resolved nothing until the user
toggled it off and on. WireGuard endpoints are affected the same way, since their
UDP socket is only re-bound by the InterfaceUpdated() half.

The added method is guarded three ways: the instance mutex (so it cannot race
Close()), the started-state check (state 1; 0 is new and 2 is closed), and the
same panic-to-error deferral Start()/Close() use, because it is invoked from a
ConnectivityManager callback where a crash would take the whole service down.

--- a/libcore/box.go
+++ b/libcore/box.go
@@ -177,6 +177,20 @@ func (b *BoxInstance) Wake() {
 	}
 }
 
+func (b *BoxInstance) ResetNetwork() {
+	b.access.Lock()
+	defer b.access.Unlock()
+
+	defer device.DeferPanicToError("box.ResetNetwork", func(err_ error) {
+		log.Println(err_.Error())
+	})
+
+	if b.state != 1 {
+		return
+	}
+	b.Box.Router().ResetNetwork()
+}
+
 func (b *BoxInstance) SetAsMain() {
 	mainInstance = b
 	goServeProtect(true)
